.TH NU 1 "October 2026" "1.1" "Nu Manual"
.SH NAME
Nu \- lightweight Bash script that creates shortcuts for SSH, SSHFS mounting, unmounting, and remote command execution.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Nu
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.I SERVERNAME USERNAME IPADDRESS|HOSTNAME
[\fIPORT\fR] [\fIREMOTE_PATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Nu
script simplifies frequent interactions with remote servers. It creates a dedicated mount point under
.I ~/mnt/
and generates three executable helper scripts in
.I ~/bin/ :

.TP
\fBSERVERNAME\fR
A shortcut for an SSH connection with agent forwarding (\-A) and X11 forwarding (\-X). The script routes subcommands (\fBping\fR, \fBmount\fR, \fBunmount\fR, \fBhelp\fR) or forwards any arguments to the remote shell preserving quotes.

.TP
\fBMountSERVERNAME\fR
A script that mounts the specified remote directory locally using
.BR sshfs (1).

.TP
\fBUnmountSERVERNAME\fR
A script that unmounts the remote directory cleanly using
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR fusermount (1),
or
.BR umount (8).

.SH USAGE
.TP
.B Nu SERVERNAME USERNAME HOST [PORT] [REMOTE_PATH]
Creates the mount point and helper scripts. Default port is 22; default remote path is /.

Example:
.IP
.EX
Nu Saruman root 65.67.51.189 2222 /
.EE

After running the command the following scripts are available:

.IP
.EX
~/bin/Saruman          # SSH shortcut & subcommand dispatcher
~/bin/MountSaruman     # SSHFS mount script
~/bin/UnmountSaruman   # Safe unmount script
.EE

.TP
.B Saruman [command]
SSH into the server or execute a remote command.

.TP
.B Saruman mount
Invokes
.BR MountSaruman .

.TP
.B Saruman unmount
Invokes
.BR UnmountSaruman .

.TP
.B Saruman ping
Runs a reachability test using
.BR ping (8).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing shortcut scripts in ~/bin/ without confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display synopsis and usage documentation.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/bin/SERVERNAME
Executable SSH shortcut script.
.TP
.I ~/bin/MountSERVERNAME
Executable SSHFS mount script.
.TP
.I ~/bin/UnmountSERVERNAME
Executable unmount helper script.
.TP
.I ~/mnt/SERVERNAME
Mount point for the remote filesystem.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR bash (1)

